                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Commander\n\nAs the commander of your learning, you should:\n\n- Be benevolent: help yourself, and help others who have not understood addition yet.\n- Be honest: do not let confidence make you underestimate or overestimate the task ahead.\n- Respect yourself: math can be understood in different ways. Find the way that suits you and follow it — we will help you find your path.\n- Use wisdom: identify your weaknesses, train them, and turn them into strengths.\n- Use sincerity: see where you need to improve, and do not build barriers because of the difficulties you find.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
